[45.586333, "o", "  ⚙ bash python3 -c \"import pip; print(pip.__file__)\"\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 16 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 --version — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 --version\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 17 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 install --dry-run --quiet requests — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 install --dry-run --quiet requests\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 18 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: pip3 list | head — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash pip3 list | head\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 19 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] bash: python3 -m pip install --dry-run wheel — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -m pip install --dry-run wheel\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 20 tool call(s) so far\r\n  glimmer-30b — 21 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ note \r\n    ✓ note — Pip module missing but dist-info remained; removed dist-info\r\nYour system Python 3.13 was present but `pip` was broken: the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory remained "]
[45.586462, "o", "in `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages` while the actual `pip/` package files were missing, so `/usr/local/bin/pip3` raised `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.\r\n\r\nFixed by forcing a reinstall via ensurepip:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nrm -rf /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info\r\npython3 -m ensurepip --upgrade\r\n```\r\n\r\nVerification:\r\n* `python3 -c \"import pip; print(pip.__file__)\"` → `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip/__init__.py`\r\n* `pip3 --version` → `pip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)`\r\n* `python3 -m pip install --dry-run wheel` succeeds\r\n\r\n`pip` is now importable and can install packages system-wide again. Consider using a virtual environment for future work to avoid system-wide permission warnings.\r\n\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=glimmer-30b tools=21 surface=305ca09d0222\r\n"]
